Flea's changes to beautiful-mermaid 1.1.3 (MIT), applied by tools/vendor-js/build.sh after npm ci with patch -p1 from the package directory:
dagre's cycle breaking in every ELK graph, label measurement from the drawn font's per-character advance tables (options.charAdvances, options.boldCharAdvances),
flowchart syntax (node ids that stop at a link, every link form with its length, ends and invisible links, first-closed subgraph membership),
ELK layout fixes (subgraph titles, bundled edges that cross nodes; a subgraph with an edge leaving it is laid out with the whole graph, as mermaid.js's dagre wrapper does, with its frame hugging its members, and the nested layout when frames would clash),
end marks Qt draws (start markers oriented auto, class diamonds referenced at their tip, a plain class link without an arrowhead) and the mirrored bottom actor row, message and note spacing of sequence diagrams.
